{
  "doc": "Ground truth for the tokens-to-answer benchmark (task 034 / 055). Each entry is one agent question with a KNOWN correct answer, plus the fixed recipe for both paths. To add a question: pick a fixture with a symbol whose answer you can state exactly; write `atlas_path` (or `session_path` for mixed MCP+native recipes), `grep` (the baseline's search pattern; omit or set `ratio_eligible: false` when there is no fair grep), `expected` (substrings that MUST appear for correctness), optional `expected_set` (complete ground-truth members for recall), and optional `grep_evidence`. `ratio_note` states WHY a question is out of the ratio (required when `ratio_eligible` is false; it reaches the report row). Every row with `expected_set` must ALSO declare precision (task 135): `precision_scope` is the path into the answering payload holding the members the answer claims — a string segment indexes a key, a `{\"field\": value}` segment picks one list element — and `precision_note` states why a shape has no such population (a ranked page, a body, a narrowed question). The harness refuses a row that declares neither, so precision can never default to green. `source: fixture` runs against a committed dir (needs the PHP adapter). `source: sample` runs against a pinned public repo named by `sample`. Private-repo symptom sets stay outside this repository (task 045).",
